PM2 Instructions

PM2 is a process manager for Node.js applications that allows you to manage and keep your apps alive forever.

1. Install PM2
To install PM2 globally, run the following command:

bash
npm install pm2 -g


2. Start an Application
To start an application with PM2, use:

bash
pm2 start app.js
Replace app.js with the entry point of your Node.js application.


3. Start Multiple Applications
To start multiple applications with specific names:

bash
pm2 start app1.js --name "app1"
pm2 start app2.js --name "app2"


4. List All Running Applications
To list all the processes currently managed by PM2:

bash
pm2 list


5. Stop an Application
To stop an application, use the name or ID:

bash
pm2 stop app1
# or using the process ID
pm2 stop 0


6. Restart an Application
To restart an application:

bash
pm2 restart app1
# or using the process ID
pm2 restart 0


7. Delete an Application
To delete an application from PM2:

bash
pm2 delete app1
# or using the process ID
pm2 delete 0


8. Monitor Applications
To monitor applications in real-time:

bash
pm2 monit


9. Save Process List
To save the current process list so that they will restart automatically after a reboot:

bash
pm2 save


10. Startup Script (auto-start PM2 on system boot)
To generate the appropriate startup script based on your OS, use:

bash
pm2 startup
Then, follow the instructions provided in the output to ensure PM2 starts after a reboot.


11. Viewing Logs
To view logs for an application:

bash
pm2 logs app1
# To view logs for all applications
pm2 logs


12. Update PM2
To update PM2 to the latest version:

bash
npm install pm2@latest -g


13. Export Process List to JSON
To export the current process list:

bash
pm2 dump
